WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:09.370
It’s been three months since we got our
hands on the 2018 MacBook Air, and our thoughts

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.249
have completely changed about it.

00:00:11.249 --> 00:00:15.099
At first, we were disappointed with a few
key problems with the new MacBook Air, and

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:20.010
we even recommended the 2017 MacBook Pro instead,
but after three months, we’ve realized that

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.670
the Air is actually the best choice for almost
everyone.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.880
I’ll explain why in just a minute.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.980
Before the new MacBook Air was released, thousands
of people were still using the old MacBook

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.020
Air, with its extremely outdated design, low-quality
display and old tech.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.800
Those people just wanted a relatively cheap
and reliable Apple laptop for everyday tasks,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.140
and it did just that.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:44.110
Now we’ve got a brand new upgraded MacBook
Air that’s up-to-date with the latest technology.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:47.220
It’s not perfect, but it’s worlds better
than the old one.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.730
As a video editor, there were a few things
the new Air lacked that were really dissapointing,

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.380
mainly the display.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:57.530
Even though it’s packing a high-resolution
Retina display, the screen itself just doesn’t

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:01.620
get very bright, and it’s not nearly as
color accurate as other MacBooks like the

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.250
2017 MacBook Pro.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.440
That’s my biggest problem with it, but I’ve
realized that it doesn’t really matter for

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:09.040
most people who don’t do photo or video
editing.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.971
And the display brightness is fine for almost
everyone, at least until you try to use it

00:01:12.971 --> 00:01:14.470
outside on a bright day.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:18.170
The second biggest problem I had was the dual-core
processor.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:21.720
Most of the laptop market has already moved
onto quad-core processors, and it’s disappointing

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.990
to see that the Air hasn’t.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:28.190
However, after using it for 3 months, I’ve
realized that it runs basically everything

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.540
you’d need on a daily basis, pretty well.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.240
Many old MacBook Air users were completely
fine with the old dual-core processors, and

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.980
the new ones even quicker.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.201
Something that really mattered was the ports.

00:01:38.201 --> 00:01:43.440
The old Air was loaded with ports and the
new one is limited to just two.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.440
It kind of sucks, but you can get a USB-C
hub on Amazon and fix that problem for relatively

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.440
cheap.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.800
The last thing to complain about is the price.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:56.549
It’s $1199, which is $200 more expensive
than the old Air, making it a bit more difficult

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:57.810
for many people to obtain.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:03.640
However, 3 months later, you easily find a
brand new 2018 MacBook Air for less than $1100.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:07.850
In fact, It’s currently on sale on Amazon
for $1079.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.480
I linked that sale in the video description
if you wanna check it out.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.910
In reality, the difference in price is well
worth it for everything you’re getting.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:19.880
Now let’s talk what’s so special about
the new MacBook Air that makes me think it’s

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.900
the best choice for almost everyone out there.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.190
First of all, the battery life is amazing.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:28.920
Apple says it lasts 2 hours longer than any
other current-gen MacBook, and trust me, they’re

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:29.920
not lying.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.610
It seems to last forever!

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.860
The updated design really makes it look like
a modern Mac, especially now that the huge

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.040
silver display bezels are gone.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:43.459
The trackpad is now much larger and more comfortable
to use, and it’s now using Force touch tech,

00:02:43.459 --> 00:02:48.190
so it doesn’t actually click, the motor
beneath it vibrates to simulate a click.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:51.470
This means that you get even clicking feel
even at the corners of the trackpad.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:52.470
The old trackpad failed in that sense.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:57.060
Some users don’t like the low key travel
of the new keyboard, but I personally don’t

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.060
mind it.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.360
It was pretty easy to get used to.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.620
It also comes with a Touch ID sensor in the
corner for logging in and buying stuff online

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:07.910
using Apple Pay, which I don’t really care
for, but it’s convenient.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.280
One huge difference you’ll notice is in
the speakers.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:12.810
They sound so much better on the new Air.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.680
The old model actually doesn’t pack any
speaker grilles, the sound just comes from

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.521
under the keyboard, and it doesn’t sound
good compared to the new speakers.

00:03:19.521 --> 00:03:22.250
You can comfortably watch TV shows using just
the integrated speakers on the new Air, since

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:30.570
vocals are now loud and clear compared to
the quite dull sound of the old Air.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:35.290
What’s great about the new Air is that it
comes with the T2 security chip, which enhances

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:39.989
security, encrypts storage on-the-fly, and
takes care of a bunch of different controllers

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:41.770
so the processor doesn’t have to.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:47.409
I personally believe that in about 6 years
Apple will release a new MacOS update that

00:03:47.409 --> 00:03:50.900
requires the T2 chip to run, basically putting
an end to the Hackintosh.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:54.409
So if you’re wanting to keep your MacBook
for a long time, this is a huge reason to

00:03:54.409 --> 00:03:55.650
buy the new Air.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:59.560
Finally, even though it only has two ports,
they’re Thunderbolt 3 ports, so they can

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:05.650
deliver 40Gb/s of throughput to connect everything
from external storage, external GPUs for gaming

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:09.159
and video editing, and even connect a 5k display.

00:04:09.159 --> 00:04:13.540
The new MacBook Air basically offers everything
the average user would need and more.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.139
From battery life and reliability to speaker
and display quality, it’s got you covered.

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:22.330
Thanks to the 8th gen processor’s modern
technology, you can even do casual video or

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.559
photo editing.

00:04:23.559 --> 00:04:26.610
It may take a bit longer than on other Macs,
but it’ll get the job done.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:31.439
Now, if you’re more serious about your professional
work, like requiring a highly color accurate

00:04:31.439 --> 00:04:35.309
display, you should look to the MacBook Pro
instead, and if you’re doing a lot of graphics

00:04:35.309 --> 00:04:40.900
intensive work like video editing, investing
the extra cash for the 15” 2018 MacBook

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.310
Pro is a wise choice.

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:45.039
It’ll easily pay for itself in time savings.

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:50.159
Overall, the 2018 MacBook Air is the Mac almost
everyone should be buying in 2019.

00:04:50.159 --> 00:04:54.740
I’m extremely satisfied with it after using
it for 3 months and I truly believe you will

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:55.740
too!

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.190
This has been Vadim with Max Tech, thanks
for watching and make sure to subscribe for

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.250
more videos like this one.

